AB  - The rapid advancement of technology has transformed education, yet students, especially in rural areas, struggle to find learning resources tailored to their needs. This paper presents a teacher-assisted, AI-powered learning recommendation platform for middle and high school students, leveraging large language models (LLMs) for personalized study plans. The platform combines the expertise of teachers with intelligent recommendation systems to deliver data-driven, personalized learning strategies to students. Through user surveys, structured teacher dashboards, and admin supervision, the application bridges resource gaps, empowers teachers, and enhances student engagement. The paper provides the system's design, teacher-student-admin interaction flows, AI methodology (based on open-source LLMs), and results for the pilot dataset deployment. The discussion reviews outcomes, challenges, and opportunities for future improvement, offering a scalable blueprint for inclusive digital transformation in rural education.
