AB  - Open-source Machine Learning (ML) models on Hugging Face (HF) are increasingly adopted across domains, yet surveys show that many lack adequate Model Card documentation, creating barriers to model reuse, auditing, and reproducibility. To address this gap, we present an automated, artifact-grounded pipeline that generates Enhanced Model Cards (EMCs) and computes quantitative reproducibility scores exclusively from official repository artifacts. The pipeline uses deterministic heuristics for artifact retrieval and a hybrid distance-based classification system to organize extracted content into predefined Model Card sections. Large Language Models (LLMs) then synthesize the classified content into structured documentation and evaluate it against a 22-point NeurIPS reproducibility checklist using constrained decoding. We validate the LLM scores against 220 human-annotated ground-truth instances. For end-to-end assessment, we benchmarked the pipeline on a stratified set of 50 models spanning all HF task tags and used an LLM-as-a-Judge framework (GPT-4.1) to compare EMCs with Original Model Cards (OMCs). EMCs achieved win rates of 86.0% for Comprehensiveness and 94.0% for Structural Clarity. The pipeline also increased the mean reproducibility score from 1.90 to 8.93 out of 22 (+7.03 points), directly quantifying the documentation gap between OMCs and information verifiably available across scattered repository artifacts. To support community adoption, the source code, curated dataset of 5,635 parsed model artifacts, and interactive web tool are publicly available.
ER  - 

