AB  - Compared to conventional Emotion Recognition in Conversations (ERC), Multimodal Emotion Recognition in Conversations (MERC) integrates multimodal information during conversational scenario modeling, thereby achieving more accurate and robust emotion recognition results that better align with human cognitive processes. This paper proposes a comprehensive review of MERC technologies. It first outlines the current research status of MERC and traces the evolutionary trajectory of deep learning-based model architectures in this field. Subsequently, it introduces representative multimodal conversational emotion datasets. The review notes two key trends: methods based on Large Language Models (LLMs) have become mainstream due to their exceptional performance and emergent capabilities, while MERC datasets are evolving toward diverse annotation schemes, natural emotions, and multilingual corpora. Finally, the paper identifies and discusses promising future research directions. This work provides a systematic and detailed survey and analysis of MERC, aiming to serve as a valuable reference for researchers in this domain.
