AB  - The evolution of large language models (LLMs) has been significantly shaped by innovations in pretraining techniques, with contrastive learning emerging as a promising strategy for enhancing contextual representation. This review paper provides an in-depth analysis of DeepSeek R1-MoDCE, an open-source pretraining framework that integrates Momentum Contrastive Learning (MoDCE) into the DeepSeek R1 architecture. We examine the theoretical foundations of MoDCE, its role in improving semantic discrimination, and how it addresses limitations in traditional masked language modeling (MLM). Furthermore, the paper benchmarks DeepSeek R1-MoDCE against established LLMs across key NLP tasks including text classification, retrieval, and few-shot learning. Through a comprehensive survey of recent literature and empirical findings, we highlight the benefits, trade-offs, and practical considerations of contrastive pretraining in real-world applications. This review aims to guide researchers and practitioners in understanding the significance of contrastive objectives in LLM development and sets the stage for future advancements in scalable, efficient language modeling.
ER  - 

