AB  - Personalized financial planning remains a critical challenge for individuals navigating complex investment environments characterized by volatile markets and diverse risk tolerances. Traditional advisory systems rely on static questionnaires and rule-based heuristics that fail to capture the dynamic behavioral and contextual dimensions of individual investors. This paper presents a Generative AI-based framework integrating large language models (LLMs) with machine learning classifiers to enable automated risk profiling and investment strategy recommendation. The proposed system combines transformer-based natural language understanding, ensemble classification, and retrieval-augmented generation to produce personalized, explainable, and adaptive financial plans. Experiments on the publicly available Survey of Consumer Finances dataset demonstrate 91.4% classification accuracy for risk profiling, outperforming all baseline recommender models on portfolio return metrics.
