AB  - Accessing and making sense of data for human decision-making has become one central task in big data systems nowadays. Traditional approaches rely heavily on technologies such as SQL, proprietary and open-source reporting software, and full-text search engines. Recent advances in Gen-AI, particularly large language models, have shown strong capability to sift through massive datasets and present insights of the data in a human-readable format. However, integrating Gen-AI into big data systems can bring other issues and concerns regarding data management and model deployment. In this survey, we provide a comprehensive overview of how LLMs and related Gen-AI technologies are transforming the ways in which humans interact with and consume data from three levels in terms of various users interaction. In addition, this manuscript illustrates recent Gen-AI advancements and propose a conceptual framework of current methodologies according to scalability, adaptability, and value. This analysis also discusses benefits of applying Gen-AI in real-world environments and examines the emerging techniques behind Gen-AI-driven big data systems. Furthermore, we highlight the key challenges and tradeoffs such as cost, privacy, and latency that must be considered before establishing Gen-AI as a reliable interface for big data. We believe that this work can serve as a general guide for researchers and practitioners seeking insights to understand the evolving relationship between Gen-AI and big data ecosystems.
ER  - 

